    "field": "Snowball Earth climate modeling",
    "problem": "Previous Snowball Earth modeling studies rarely simulated the entire transition from a present-day climate, instead using simplified initial conditions to identify trigger points, which left the full dynamics, timing, and point of unstoppable glaciation of the transition itself uncharacterized.",
    "method": "We use the coupled atmosphere-ocean general circulation model ECHAM5/MPI-OM to investigate the transition to a modern Snowball Earth by starting from the present-day climate and applying an abrupt decrease of total solar irradiance (TSI).",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the transition from the present-day climate to a modern Snowball Earth using the coupled atmosphere-ocean general circulation model ECHAM5/MPI-OM by analyzing the bifurcation point, transition times, and associated climate dynamics.",
