            "paragraph": "The ocean component MPI-OM employs the primitive equations on an orthogonal curvilinear C-grid (Arakawa and Lamb 1977), with the North Pole shifted to Greenland to avoid a singularity at the geographical North Pole. The grid South Pole is located over Antarctica. In the vertical, the model employs unevenly spaced z-levels with the bottom topography being resolved by way of partial grid cells (Wolff et al. 1997).",
